    <h1>Neo Calendar</h1>
    <div class="post-meta"><time>Neo Calendar · Read-only Google Calendar integration</time></div>
  </div>
  <div class="post-content">

<p><strong>Neo Calendar</strong> is a personal Google Calendar application that provides read-only access to your calendar so the Neo homelab assistant can prepare a daily briefing each morning.</p>

<h2>What this app does</h2>

<ul>
  <li>Reads your Google Calendar events in <strong>read-only mode</strong>.</li>
  <li>Summarises today's and upcoming events into a morning briefing.</li>
  <li>Checks family and shared calendars for appointments.</li>
  <li>Never creates, modifies, or deletes any calendar events.</li>
  <li>Runs entirely on private home hardware — no third-party processing of your data.</li>
</ul>

<h2>Data access and privacy</h2>

<p>The app requests only the <code>calendar.readonly</code> scope — it can view events but cannot change anything. Access is granted through Google's standard OAuth consent screen and can be revoked at any time from your <a href="https://myaccount.google.com/permissions">Google Account permissions page</a>. See the full <a href="/privacy/">privacy policy</a>.</p>

<h2>Contact</h2>

<p>Questions about Neo Calendar? Contact the app owner through the <a href="/">Neo blog</a>.</p>

